 /*
- * SWEET (polaris) touch: Synaptics S3330 on QUPv3 SE14.
+ * SWEET (polaris) touch: Synaptics S3330 bit-banged I2C over GPIO 33/34.
  *
- * The Mi Mix 2S touch controller (S3330, JDI incell panel) is on GENI I2C
- * SE14 (DT qupv3_se14_i2c, i2c@a98000, 7-bit address 0x20), with reset on
- * TLMM GPIO 99, IRQ on GPIO 125 and the I/O rail (tp_vddio_vreg) enabled by
- * GPIO 23 (SOUTH pin bank). The GENI I2C firmware is the one XBL leaves
- * loaded (protocol 3, 32-bit FIFOs), exactly what the vendor kernel expects;
- * this driver does no firmware/config upload and no panel-rail writes.
+ * The Mi Mix 2S uses a JDI FHD (NT35596S) panel with the Synaptics S3330
+ * touch controller at 7-bit address 0x20.  The controller is on QUPv3 SE14
+ * (i2c@a98000), but XBL loads a GSI-only I2C firmware there: the GENI FIFO
+ * interface is disabled (GENI_IF_FIFO_DISABLE_RO bit 0 set), which is why
+ * the FIFO transport in the previous patch could not talk to the chip.
+ * Instead of porting GSI/IOMMU DMA, this driver muxes the two QUP pins back
+ * to GPIO and drives I2C in software.  The bus is open-drain with board
+ * pull-ups (the DT active state is bias-disable); the TLMM pull-up is also
+ * enabled.  Everything else is unchanged: tp_vddio on GPIO 23, reset on
+ * GPIO 99, IRQ on GPIO 125 (polled, not used).
  *
- * The controller speaks Synaptics RMI4.  A register access is:
- *   write 0xFF, page      (page-select register)
- *   write <low address>, then repeated START + read (read)
- *   write <low address>, <data>                    (write)
- * The PDT is scanned for F01 (identification) and F12 (2D touch); F12
- * reporting is enabled with ctrl28 = 0xff and the data registers are polled
- * (10 ms) into the SweetHIDTouch service.  The IRQ line is only configured,
- * not used, so a missed edge can never wedge input.
+ * The controller speaks Synaptics RMI4:
+ *   write 0xFF, page   (page-select register)
+ *   write <low addr>, then repeated START + read
+ *   write <low addr>, <data>
+ * The driver scans the PDT for F01/F12, enables F12 reporting with ctrl28 =
+ * 0xff and polls the F12 data registers into SweetHIDTouch.
  *
- * Coordinates are scaled from the F12 sensor maximum to the 1080x2160 panel
- * (SweetHID.cpp presents that same native size under sweetfb_native=1).
+ * GPIO 33 is tried as SCL and GPIO 34 as SDA first; if the controller does
+ * not acknowledge, the pair is swapped and probed again (the QUP pin order
+ * is not documented in the DT).
